other-languages.lust:1:1  Lust calls it truth: truth alive = true;
other-languages.lust:2:1  Lust asks questions instead of if: is hp 0? then { }
other-languages.lust:2:7  Lust has no ==. To check if two things are the same, ask: is a b?
other-languages.lust:2:29  Lust uses or instead of else: } or { }
other-languages.lust:3:1  Lust has one loop: loop (hp > 0) { }
other-languages.lust:4:1  Lust uses give to hand back a value.
other-languages.lust:5:1  put the type first, like int lives = 3;
other-languages.lust:6:1  Lust makes functions with do.
other-languages.lust:7:7  Lust calls it nothing.
